# 025 — output field-contract byte-identity corrections
#
# Comparison of my function OUTPUT dict keys against the original's real field
# contract (RE'd from aside-arm64.bin machine code + confirmed by the extension
# consumer, which was written against the original API) found 7 functions whose
# output field names/shapes did NOT match the original. All corrected:
#
# 1) getLanguageSettings
#    was: {acceptLanguages, selectedLanguages}
#    now: {preferredLanguages:[...], spellCheckEnabled, spellCheckSupported}
#    (RE 0x406ed48: fields preferredLanguages/spellCheckEnabled/spellCheckSupported;
#     spellCheckEnabled read from Chromium pref browser.enable_spellchecking)
#
# 2) getSupportedLanguages item
#    was: {languageCode, displayName}
#    now: {code, displayName, nativeDisplayName}
#    (ext matcher He/E: item.code, item.displayName, item.nativeDisplayName;
#     "languageCode" in binary is billing/offer code, unrelated)
#
# 3) getDefaultBrowserState
#    was: {isDefault, canBeDefault}
#    now: {isDefault, canSet, policyDisabled}
#    (ext reads t?.isDefault, n?.canSet, t?.policyDisabled)
#
# 4) setAsDefaultBrowser
#    was: {isDefault}
#    now: {isDefault, canSet, policyDisabled}   (same shape as getDefaultBrowserState;
#          ext replaces defaultBrowserState with this result)
#
# 5) getDockState / addToDock
#    was: {isInDock, supported}
#    now: {isAdded, canAdd}
#    ("isInDock" absent from binary; ext reads i.isAdded, i.canAdd)
#
# 6) getSearchEngines (asideBrowserPreferences)
#    was: {engines:[{id,name,keyword,isDefault}]}
#    now: {searchEngines:[{id,shortName,keyword,isDefault}], defaultEngineId}
#    (ext reads n?.searchEngines, n?.defaultEngineId, engine.id/.isDefault/.keyword)
#
# 7) getSearchEngines (asideOmnibox) — rich engine objects
#    was: {engines:[{id,name,keyword,isDefault}]}
#    now: {engines:[{id,shortName,keyword,isDefault,featuredByPolicy,faviconUrl,
#          searchUrlTemplate,suggestUrlTemplate,imageUrlTemplate,
#          imageTranslateUrlTemplate,newTabUrl,contextualSearchUrl}],
#          defaultEngineId, loaded}
#    (RE 0x405aef8: engines/defaultEngineId/loaded + these engine fields; shortName not name)
#
# Confirmed already correct (no change): getSyncStatus {isSyncing},
#   getKeepTasksRunningState {enabled}, getProfileContext
#   {profileId,profilePath,profileIndex,boundUserId,boundAccountId}.
#
# Platform note: checkForUpdates has no Linux original (macOS Sparkle-style
#   updater only). Field vocabulary aligned to the binary ({state, available});
#   true byte-identity is not achievable for an OS-specific updater on Linux.
#
# id types unified to string (base::NumberToString) to match the string
#   engineId param of setDefaultSearchEngine and the ext's id comparisons.
#
# See overlay/ for the full post-change files.

# 8) omnibox addFileContext / addTabContext result
#    was: addFileContext {contextToken};  addTabContext {contextToken, tabId}
#    now: both {ok:true, contextToken}   (shared context-add result {ok,contextToken,errorType?}, RE 0x406a7c8)
#    (ext gates on (await addFileContext(...))?.ok; result builder has no tabId)

# 9) browser_import getImportSources / getImportProgress
#    getImportSources: was {name, importerType, importItems}  (importerType/importItems ABSENT from binary)
#                      now {id, name, profiles:[{id, name, lastUsedAt?}]}  (RE: id/name/profiles present)
#    getImportProgress: was {jobId, completed, progress:100}
#                       now {jobId, progress, state}  (RE 0x4051430: jobId/progress/state/currentDataKind/errorMessage/sourceId;
#                       ext checks state==="succeeded"; "completed" is not a field)
#    getProfiles (asideAccount): CONFIRMED correct — schema ProfileInfo {profileIndex,name,isCurrent,isLocked} byte-identical.
